<service>
  <id>pios-frontend</id>
  <name>PIOS Frontend</name>
  <description>PIOS frontend, served from the production build via a small custom Node server (frontend/server/serve.mjs), replacing `vite preview` -- Growth Loops TZ v1, Phase 1 (docs/PIOS_GROWTH_LOOPS_TZ_V1.md Section 1): `vite preview` could not inject the per-driver &lt;meta&gt; tags a shared personal link needs for a real WhatsApp/Telegram/VK preview card. Runs `node.exe` directly against the server script rather than through npm.cmd, so WinSW's stop signal reaches the actual Node process instead of an intermediate cmd shell.</description>
  <executable>C:\Program Files\nodejs\node.exe</executable>
  <arguments>server\serve.mjs</arguments>
  <workingdirectory>C:\Projects\PIOS-Foundation_v1.0\frontend</workingdirectory>
  <!-- No HOST/PORT/PUBLIC_ORIGIN env override below: serve.mjs's own
       defaults already match every constraint the old vite preview
       flags encoded.

       HOST 0.0.0.0, not 127.0.0.1 or vite's own "localhost" default: this
       machine's IPv6 loopback is broken (a third-party VPN/proxy TUN
       adapter intercepting the loopback address, diagnosed earlier this
       session), and O-2 requires phone/LAN reachability, not just
       localhost.

       PORT 4173, not 5173: PIOS_PILOT_INFRASTRUCTURE_DECISION.md Section
       4's own port for the tunnelled pilot surface
       (docs/PIOS_NAMED_TUNNEL_DEPLOYMENT.md). Unlike vite preview's own
       strictPort flag, serve.mjs has no competing dev server default to
       fall back to, so there is nothing to silently bind instead.

       PUBLIC_ORIGIN defaults to https://home-pc.tail385153.ts.net, the
       same Tailscale Funnel hostname vite.config.ts's own
       preview.allowedHosts already allows, used only to build the
       absolute og:url/og:image a link-preview crawler requires. -->
  <log mode="none"/>
  <onfailure action="restart" delay="30 sec"/>
  <onfailure action="restart" delay="60 sec"/>
  <onfailure action="restart" delay="120 sec"/>
  <resetfailure>24 hours</resetfailure>
  <startmode>Automatic</startmode>
</service>
